senses.gloss:
dṛṣṭa-,
(1) short for dṛṣṭadharma or ˚dhārmika, in a cpd.: (sarvadharmāṇāṃ) … dṛṣṭasukhasaṃsthānām abhilāpya-(read with Tib. an-abhi˚) -gati-viśeṣāḥ Laṅk 〔18.7〕 (prose), innumerable different courses of all states-of-existence which are based on (saṃstha) the pleasures of the visible (world). Suzuki fails utterly to understand the passage. For the phrase dṛṣṭa dharma, see next;
(2) perhaps = dṛṣṭi, false view: āya-vyaya-dṛṣṭābhiniveśena Laṅk 〔174.12〕 (see s.vv. āya and abhiniveśa); the alternative would be to emend to ˚dṛṣṭy-abhi˚.
